meta {
  name: Get Related Products Subpath (Bug - Empty)
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

get {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/REPLACE_WITH_PRODUCT_ID/relationships/REPLACE_WITH_RELATIONSHIP_ID/related-products
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-15 against the same disposable scratch products
  and relationship type as "Create Product Relationship Link.bru" on
  "David's Dev Account".

  ## Real bug: this subpath returns empty despite a confirmed live link
  `GET /products/{product_id}/relationships/{relationship_id}/related-products`
  is documented by the spec as the way to list which products are on the
  other end of a relationship link. Tested immediately after "Create
  Product Relationship Link.bru" successfully linked product A to product
  B (confirmed three independent ways: the create response itself, the
  full product's `product_relationships` field, and
  `GET /related-products?product_id=<A>` all show the link) -- but this
  dedicated subpath returned `{"data": [], "errors": []}`, empty, both
  immediately and on a retry a few seconds later (ruling out simple
  read-after-write/indexing lag). **This looks like a genuine bug in the
  new endpoint**, not a naming/discovery mistake -- the sibling identity
  endpoint one level up (`.../relationships/{relationship_id}`, see "Get
  Product Relationship by ID.bru") correctly reflects the link's
  existence; only this specific `related-products` collection view is
  wrong.

  Use `GET /related-products?product_id=<id>` (the top-level search
  endpoint, correctly scoped when filtered -- see "Get Related Products
  (Top-Level).bru") as the reliable way to find which products are
  related to a given one, until this subpath is fixed. Report to Plytix.

  The single-item variant, `GET .../related-products/{related_product_id}`,
  was also tested and 404s even for the real, just-linked product --
  consistent with the collection view being empty (see the second
  example below).
}

example {
  name: Get Related Products Subpath - Empty Despite Confirmed Link (Bug)
  description: Real response captured 2026-09-15, immediately after "Create Product Relationship Link.bru" confirmed the link exists via three other independent checks.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6aa97b2ca30ca5945169a23f/relationships/6aa97b2ca30ca5945169a23e/related-products
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 200
      text: OK
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [],
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: Get Related Product by ID Subpath - Not Found Despite Confirmed Link (Bug)
  description: Real response captured 2026-09-15, same underlying bug as the collection view above -- the single-item lookup also can't find the just-linked related product.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6aa97b2ca30ca5945169a23f/relationships/6aa97b2ca30ca5945169a23e/related-products/6aa97b2da30ca5945169a240
    method: get
    mode: none
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Accept: application/json
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 404
      text: Not Found
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [],
          "errors": [
            {
              "name": "NotFoundError",
              "description": "Association (product_id=6aa97b2ca30ca5945169a23f, relationship_id=6aa97b2ca30ca5945169a23e, related_product_id=6aa97b2da30ca5945169a240) not found"
            }
          ]
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
